  "dcterms:title": "Harmonizome",
  "dcterms:description": "The Harmonizome, a collection of processed gene- and protein-attribute datasets mined from over a hundred publicly available resources, produced by the Ma'ayan Laboratory at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai. The brick's download script (stages/01_download.py) is the official Harmonizome downloader that fetches gene_attribute matrices and gene-set libraries from https://maayanlab.cloud/static/hdfs/harmonizome/data/. Because Harmonizome aggregates >100 upstream resources (e.g. COSMIC, KEGG, TRANSFAC, CTD), individual component datasets may carry their own additional restrictions.",
